# Atlas runtime (default compose): two independent Bybit accounts.
# Prefer the localhost console; it writes mode-0600 files to <userdir>/secrets/.
# Environment alternative: CAP_DEMO_KEY, CAP_DEMO_SECRET, CAP_LIVE_KEY, CAP_LIVE_SECRET.
# Do not place actual credentials in this tracked example.
# Demo means Bybit Demo Trading, never Testnet. Live is switched explicitly in the UI.

# Legacy research stack only (compose.legacy.yml):
# Keys do not live in the repo. Use Vault / sops (PHASE-BUILD step 0.1.2).
# This file documents names only. Do not paste live credentials here.

# Gateway (signer process only; the desk never reads these). Values via Vault / secrets manager.
#   BYBIT_API_KEY      — key with trade permission only, no withdrawal, IP-whitelisted
#   BYBIT_API_SECRET   — its secret
#   BYBIT_MODE         — demo | testnet | live_sub | live_main (default demo).
#                        demo = Bybit Demo Trading (api-demo.bybit.com, mainnet data,
#                        simulated funds) — the desk's demo phase venue; keys come from the
#                        Demo Trading page, not from the main account.
#                        testnet = legacy paper venue (prices do not match the mainnet tape).
#                        User mode "demo" pairs with demo|testnet keys only; "live" with live_*.
# Alternative: <userdir>/secrets/bybit.json {"api_key","api_secret","mode"} with mode 0600.
